<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hồ Quý Ly</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1336">1336</a>–c. 1407</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Ho Quy Ly</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hồ Quý Ly was a powerful minister of the Trần dynasty who deposed the last Trần emperor in 1400 and founded the Hồ dynasty. He carried out radical reforms, issuing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paper-money">paper money</a>, limiting landholdings and building a stone citadel at Tây Đô. The Ming used his usurpation as a pretext to invade in 1406 and captured him in 1407.</p></div>
